<http://data.silknow.org/object/761420fa-a9d7-353a-a9a5-410b2ada1298/observation/1>
        a                   crmsci:S4_Observation ;
        ecrm:P2_has_type    <http://data.silknow.org/observation/technical-observation> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note    "Dress (bodice and skirt) of ribbed purple silk fastened with buttons needlewoven in silk over a wooden mould. The skirt is ruched with a bustle and flounces. The jacket bodice has a revered coat lapel front and bow detail and is lined with silk and whalebone strips."@en ;
        crmsci:O8_observed  <http://data.silknow.org/object/761420fa-a9d7-353a-a9a5-410b2ada1298> .

<http://data.silknow.org/event/52bd460c-6264-329c-b257-65bae52dc46b>
        a                              ecrm:E8_Acquisition ;
        rdfs:comment                   "RF number is 1922/730.\n\nThis dress, and 4 others (sequence T.49 to 53&A-1922) were donated by the then Marchioness of Bristol, Geraldine Georgiana Mary Hervey (née Anson) (1843-25/1/1927), as coming from her mother's wedding trousseau of 1873. However, there may be a misunderstanding where this provenance is concerned, as Geraldine Hervey's own wedding was 4 March 1862; her mothers' was 30 November 1830. The information is from a letter of the donor to the Museum. While the dresses certainly could have been part of a family trousseau, it would not have been that of the Marchioness nor her mother's."@en ;
        ecrm:P14_carried_out_by        <http://data.silknow.org/actor/7cd75f97-2842-38f7-9854-18c314de234c> ;
        ecrm:P22_transferred_title_to  <http://data.silknow.org/actor/f0577f91-f887-3019-bf88-f9e5ba019390> ;
        ecrm:P23_transferred_title_from
                "Given by the Marchioness of Bristol" ;
        ecrm:P24_transferred_title_of  <http://data.silknow.org/object/761420fa-a9d7-353a-a9a5-410b2ada1298> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note               "RF number is 1922/730.\n\nThis dress, and 4 others (sequence T.49 to 53&A-1922) were donated by the then Marchioness of Bristol, Geraldine Georgiana Mary Hervey (née Anson) (1843-25/1/1927), as coming from her mother's wedding trousseau of 1873. However, there may be a misunderstanding where this provenance is concerned, as Geraldine Hervey's own wedding was 4 March 1862; her mothers' was 30 November 1830. The information is from a letter of the donor to the Museum. While the dresses certainly could have been part of a family trousseau, it would not have been that of the Marchioness nor her mother's."@en .

